---
Audit and fix all strncpy calls.

strncpy does not guarantee null-termination when source is longer than
the buffer. All uses must explicitly null-terminate the destination.

## Acceptance Criteria
- [x] Every strncpy call followed by explicit null-termination (buf[size-1] = '\0')
- [x] Or replaced with snprintf which always null-terminates
- [x] No buffer overflow possible from unterminated strings
- [x] Applies to all source files

## Test Plan
- [ ] grep all strncpy calls, verify each has null-termination
- [ ] Test with strings exactly at buffer size, verify no overflow
- [ ] Test with strings longer than buffer, verify truncation + null termination
